From 95bdac91e3fd1c0bfe1fd9f8e9be36db1cf7b6bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jatniel <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:41:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Play under the running profile's name

A profile's name was only a label in profiles.json. The name a server sees comes
from Options::player_name, which never looked at profiles: it read the offline
name kept in horizon-player.txt, generated once as Player + 5 digits. So a
profile called "Ana" joined as Player5480.

The running profile's name is now the player's name (below --name, the
environment and a signed-in account, which still win), read from the index each
time so a rename or a profile switch counts at once. The built-in profile keeps
its generated offline name as before. A profile name is a name a player can have
in Minecraft (1 to 16 printable characters, no spaces), so the name box checks
it as it is typed; profiles named before this keep working and play under the
nearest valid name.

A generated name that can't be written to disk is now the same name every time
it is asked for in a run, instead of a new one on each join.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
